error: `prefix` is not supported. Stripping a prefix means rebuilding the row under different column names, and the failure a user then sees names the stripped column ("no column \"id\"") rather than the real one ("author_id") — a worse error than the one it saves. Use `#[keelson(flatten)]` with a nested struct whose fields carry `#[keelson(rename = "author_id")]`, which reads the same row and reports real column names
